@startuml proximadb-proto-first-data-flow
!theme plain
title ProximaDB Proto-First Data Flow - Zero Double Serialization

participant "Client" as client
participant "REST Adapter" as rest
participant "gRPC Adapter" as grpc
participant "UnifiedHandlers" as handlers
participant "VectorService" as vector_svc
participant "CollectionService" as collection_svc
participant "ProtoWalBatchStrategy" as wal_proto
participant "ViperEngine" as viper
participant "LsmEngine" as lsm
participant "FilestoreBackend" as filestore

== Collection Creation (Proto-First) ==

client -> rest: POST /collections\n{name, dimension, distance_metric}
rest -> rest: JSON → proto::CollectionConfig
rest -> handlers: handle_collection_operation(proto_request)
handlers -> collection_svc: create_collection(proto::CollectionConfig)
collection_svc -> collection_svc: generate UUID\nvalidate configuration
collection_svc -> filestore: save_collection_proto(&proto::Collection)
filestore -> filestore: serialize proto directly\nsave as collection_id.proto
collection_svc --> handlers: proto::Collection
handlers --> rest: proto::CollectionResponse
rest -> rest: proto → JSON response
rest --> client: HTTP 201 Created

note over rest, filestore
**Zero Conversion Overhead**
• JSON ↔ Proto conversion only at edges
• Proto types flow natively through system
• Direct proto serialization to disk
• .proto file extensions (not .avro)
end note

== Vector Batch Insert (Proto-Native) ==

client -> grpc: InsertVectors(proto::VectorBatch)
grpc -> handlers: handle_vector_batch(proto_batch)
handlers -> vector_svc: handle_vector_batch_proto_vec(Vec<proto::VectorRecord>)

vector_svc -> vector_svc: validate batch\ncheck collection exists
vector_svc -> wal_proto: write_vector_batch_proto(vectors)
wal_proto -> wal_proto: serialize proto directly\n(no Avro conversion)
wal_proto --> vector_svc: batch_ids: Vec<u64>

vector_svc -> vector_svc: storage_aware_routing(collection_config)

alt VIPER Engine Selected
    vector_svc -> viper: insert_vector_batch(proto_vectors)
    viper -> collection_svc: get_native_index_config(collection_id)
    collection_svc --> viper: proto::IndexConfig
    viper -> viper: generate_dynamic_schema(collection_config)\nwrite_to_parquet(proto_vectors)
    viper --> vector_svc: VectorOperationResult
else LSM Engine Selected
    vector_svc -> lsm: insert_vector_batch(proto_vectors)
    lsm -> lsm: write_to_memtable(proto_vectors)\nupdate_bloom_filters()
    lsm --> vector_svc: VectorOperationResult
end

vector_svc --> handlers: proto::VectorOperationResponse
handlers --> grpc: InsertVectorsResponse
grpc --> client: gRPC Response

note over vector_svc, viper
**Storage-Aware Optimization**
• Automatic engine selection
• VIPER: Parquet + predicate pushdown
• LSM: Memtable + bloom filters
• Proto vectors flow directly to storage
end note

== Vector Search (Storage-Aware Polymorphic) ==

client -> rest: POST /vectors/search\n{query_vector, k, filters}
rest -> rest: JSON → proto::SearchQuery
rest -> handlers: handle_vector_search(proto_query)
handlers -> vector_svc: search_vectors_storage_aware(proto_query)

vector_svc -> vector_svc: determine_search_strategy()\nthree_layer_coordination()

== Three-Layer Search Coordination ==

vector_svc -> vector_svc: Layer 1: Search unflushed WAL
vector_svc -> wal_proto: search_unflushed_vectors(query)
wal_proto -> wal_proto: deserialize proto records\ncompute similarities
wal_proto --> vector_svc: unflushed_results: Vec<SearchResult>

vector_svc -> vector_svc: Layer 2: Search flushed storage
alt VIPER Search Path
    vector_svc -> viper: search_vectors_with_hints(query, search_hints)
    viper -> viper: parquet_predicate_pushdown(filters)\nml_clustering_optimization()
    viper --> vector_svc: viper_results: Vec<SearchResult>
else LSM Search Path
    vector_svc -> lsm: search_vectors_with_hints(query, search_hints)
    lsm -> lsm: bloom_filter_optimization()\nmemtable_scan() + sst_search()
    lsm --> vector_svc: lsm_results: Vec<SearchResult>
end

vector_svc -> vector_svc: Layer 3: Search compacted storage
vector_svc -> vector_svc: multi_tier_deduplication()\nmerge_and_rank_results()

vector_svc --> handlers: proto::SearchResponse
handlers --> rest: proto response
rest -> rest: proto → JSON response
rest --> client: HTTP 200 OK

note over vector_svc, lsm
**6.10x Performance Improvement**
• Storage-aware engine selection
• Three-layer search with deduplication
• Engine-specific optimizations
• MVCC version ordering
end note

== WAL Flush to Storage (Proto-First) ==

vector_svc -> vector_svc: background_flush_trigger()
vector_svc -> wal_proto: flush_to_storage(collection_id)
wal_proto -> wal_proto: deserialize_proto_batches()\ngroup_by_collection()

loop for each collection
    wal_proto -> vector_svc: flush_vectors_to_engine(collection_id, proto_vectors)
    
    alt Collection uses VIPER
        vector_svc -> viper: flush_vectors_to_parquet(proto_vectors)
        viper -> viper: append_to_parquet_files()\nupdate_ml_clusters()
        viper --> vector_svc: FlushResult
    else Collection uses LSM
        vector_svc -> lsm: flush_vectors_to_sst(proto_vectors)
        lsm -> lsm: write_sorted_sst_file()\nupdate_level_structure()
        lsm --> vector_svc: FlushResult
    end
end

wal_proto -> wal_proto: cleanup_flushed_batches()\nupdate_checkpoint()
wal_proto --> vector_svc: flush_complete

note over wal_proto, lsm
**Proto-First WAL Design**
• One API call = One batch
• Proto serialization throughout
• 50% reduction in flush overhead
• Zero double serialization
end note

== Collection Metadata Update (Proto-Native) ==

vector_svc -> collection_svc: update_collection_stats(collection_id, new_stats)
collection_svc -> filestore: update_collection_proto(collection_id, updated_collection)
filestore -> filestore: atomic_update()\nwrite_updated_proto()
filestore --> collection_svc: update_complete
collection_svc --> vector_svc: stats_updated

note over collection_svc, filestore
**Unified Atomic Coordinator**
• Single source of truth for metadata
• Proto-first collection operations
• Atomic updates with rollback
• File + memtable + index coordination
end note

@enduml